# Optional overrides. Copy to .env only if you need one; the server runs fine without this file.
#
# There are no API keys here on purpose. The server reads keys, base URLs and models straight
# from the local CLI configs:
#   Claude Code: ~/.claude/settings.json ("env": ANTHROPIC_AUTH_TOKEN / ANTHROPIC_API_KEY / ANTHROPIC_BASE_URL)
#   Codex:       ~/.codex/config.toml (model_provider, base_url, model) + ~/.codex/auth.json (OPENAI_API_KEY)
# Point elsewhere with CLAUDE_CONFIG_DIR / CODEX_HOME.

# Per-tier model, as "anthropic:<model>" or "openai:<model>". A choice made on the settings page
# (/settings) takes precedence over these.
# MODEL_DIALOGUE=anthropic:claude-opus-5-5
# MODEL_PLANNER=anthropic:claude-sonnet-5-5
# MODEL_CHEAP=openai:gpt-6.1-sol

# Server-side refusal fallback (Claude, beta): auto = only when talking to api.anthropic.com directly.
# LLM_REFUSAL_FALLBACK=auto

# Cost caps in USD (estimates). Per village per game day: over budget, calls drop to the cheap tier.
# Global per real day: over cap, calls are refused.
# LLM_VILLAGE_DAILY_BUDGET_USD=1
# LLM_GLOBAL_DAILY_CAP_USD=5

# Listen on the local network (phones on the same Wi-Fi), behind a pairing token. Or: pnpm start:lan
# ELMSFORD_LAN=1

# PORT=8787
# DATABASE_PATH=./data/elmsford.sqlite
